<title>GERMANY: Germany to reduce 1997 budget deficit.</title>
<headline>Germany to reduce 1997 budget deficit.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government has agreed budget measures to reduce its 1997 federal deficit to 53.3 billion marks from the planned 56.5 billion marks, the budget committee of the lower house of parliament said on Friday.</p>
<p>Coalition parties agreed the steps, which rely primarily on higher revenues from privatisations, in a budget committee session late on Thursday, committee members said.</p>
<p>Federal outlays in 1997 will remain slightly below 440 billion marks, as originally planned, they said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
